changelog: |
  0.1.1 — the panel says when the console's operator ended the sharing.

  * The console's Assist page lists the fleet pages sharing themselves and can
    end one. The panel then reads "Sharing was ended from the console", apart
    from a session the console dropped as idle or lost in a restart.

  0.1.0 — the console's page bridge, made portable (ADR 0014).

  * ONE FILE, THREE LAYERS. fleet-assist.js is `FleetAssistCore` (the page's
    rules and its eight actions, usable without the panel), the link to the
    Harness Console on this machine, and `<fleet-assist>` (the shadow-DOM
    panel: share, Look / Ask first / Act, Allow and Deny, a pairing code).
    Zero dependencies; nothing is sent until the person opens the panel.
  * THE SAME RULES AS THE CONSOLE'S OWN PAGE. A control is a ref from a
    snapshot, never a selector; nothing is clicked or typed inside a modal
    dialog or behind an open one; a secret field is never read or filled; a
    link that leaves the site is the person's. tools/console/
    test_page_bridge.py holds the kit, the console's page and the broker to
    one set of lists.
  * A SITE OF PLAIN PAGES KEEPS ITS SESSION. Navigating loads a new address;
    the shared session is picked up on the next page (sessionStorage, this tab
    only), and the broker hands a command to the newest poll only.
  * ADAPTERS for Jekyll, MkDocs, plain HTML, Django templates, React (Vite)
    and Next.js. Each is off outside development unless the repo says otherwise.
  * A fleet page is reached by PAIRING only: a Claude Code session presents
    the single-use code the panel shows. The page holds no console token.
